.TH RMDIR 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove empty directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rmdir
.RB [ \-p ]
.I dir
.RI [ dir ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rmdir
removes each empty directory named by a
.I dir
operand. Multiple operands are processed in turn; an error on one
operand does not stop the rest from being attempted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
After removing
.IR dir ,
also remove each ancestor directory named by the leading components of
.IR dir 's
pathname, working upward one component at a time. Ascent stops
quietly, without an error, as soon as an ancestor is found to be
non-empty or no further ancestor remains to strip \(em removing
.I dir
itself must still succeed regardless. Any other failure encountered
while removing an ancestor (for example, a permission error) is
reported as a diagnostic and does count as an error for that operand.
.PP
.B \-p
is recognized only as a literal, unadorned argument; it cannot be
combined with other letters in the same argument. Any other argument
beginning with
.B \-
(other than
.BR \-\- ,
which ends option parsing) is rejected as an invalid option.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I dir
A pathname of an empty directory to remove.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every
.I dir
operand was removed successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred: an invalid option, no
.I dir
operand at all, or a failure removing one or more of the named
directories (or, under
.BR \-p ,
one of their ancestors). Exactly one nonzero status is used for all of
these cases.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR rm (1)
